Apple today released new firmware for the AirPods Pro 2, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods-pro/">AirPods Pro 3</a>, AirPods 4, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods-max/">AirPods Max 2</a>. The firmware is available for all of the above devices, and it will enable support for new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> features. The firmware has a build number of 9A348.<br/>
 <br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/AirPods-Pro-Beta-Firmware-2.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1060562" /><br/>
In &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-27/">iPadOS 27</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a>, Apple is adding a new AirPods interface, a slider for Adaptive mode, and support for custom EQ. AirPods are also compatible with the new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI.<br/>
 <br/>
